# ADOS Core Rules

## Mission

ADOS is an Enterprise AI Operating System.

Always preserve the architecture.

Never duplicate existing functionality.

Prefer extending existing modules instead of creating new ones.

## Code

Generate production-ready code.

Avoid temporary solutions.

Keep files modular.

Use existing services whenever possible.

## Architecture

Respect the current project structure.

Do not rename or move modules unless explicitly requested.

Do not modify unrelated files.

## Documentation

When adding a feature:

- update documentation;
- update architecture if required;
- keep changes consistent.

## Testing

Do not reduce test coverage.

Generate tests for new functionality whenever appropriate.

## Final Check

Before completing a task:

- verify imports;
- verify typing;
- verify architecture consistency;
- verify tests.